# Shell scripts run on the server side and are executed by bash, which will not
# tolerate a CR at the end of a line.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Unity's own serialized files: stored byte-for-byte, with no line-ending
# conversion in either direction.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so without this git converts these on
# checkout and re-checks them on every status. Unity rewrites them whenever the
# Editor opens, saves a scene, or edits the tag and build-settings lists, and the
# two conventions disagreed often enough that ProjectSettings/*.asset sat in
# `git status` as modified with an empty `git diff` -- a permanent false positive
# that hides a real edit when one does happen.
#
# Nothing here is merged by hand or read across platforms, so normalization buys
# this repository nothing. Whatever the Editor writes is what git stores.
*.asset  -text
*.unity  -text
*.prefab -text
*.meta   -text
*.mat    -text
*.mask   -text
*.inputactions -text
